The '''Separatist Senate Building''', also known as the '''Separatist Parliament Building''', was located in [[Raxus Secundus]]' [[capital]] [[city]], [[Raxulon]], and served as the headquarters for the [[Separatist Senate|Senate]] of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]].

==Description==
[[File:Ciscapitalcity.png|thumb|left|200px|200px|The building in the middle of the urban sprawl.]]
The Separatist Senate Building,<ref name="Concept">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/heroes-on-both-sides-concept-art-gallery|text="Heroes on Both Sides" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref> also known as the Separatist Parliament Building or Separatist Parliament headquarters, was an ornate building located at the heart of [[Raxulon]],<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> located in the middle of the [[capital]] [[city]].<ref name="Heroes" /> The structure soared above the urban landscape,<ref name="VE" /> with circular streets encompassing it and a plaza with trees nearly encompassed by the complex. Inside the main building was the Senate chamber, with rows of representatives seated on each side of the main podium. [[Count]] [[Dooku]] would appear in either [[hologram]] form or in person to preside over important decisions.<ref name="Heroes" />

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Raxus_concept_Presley.png|thumb|200px|Concept art of the Senate Building by Pat Presley]]
The Separatist Senate building first appeared in "[[Heroes on Both Sides]],"<ref name="Heroes" /> the tenth episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|third season]], which aired on [[November 19]], [[2010]].<ref name="TCW Episode Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Episode Guide]]''</ref> While not named in the episode itself, the building was identified in a piece of concept art released as part of the accompanying Episode Guide on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Concept" /> Concept art of the Separatist Senate Building's exterior was drawn by [[Pat Presley]], who took inspiration from art by [[Ralph McQuarrie]].<ref name="Presley Concept">{{WebCite|url=https://www.behance.net/gallery/13768509/Star-Wars-The-Clone-Wars|text=Star Wars: The Clone Wars|author=Pat Presley|work=[https://www.behance.net/phattro Pat Presley]|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/OQFTD}}</ref>

